# fail-open-guard ratchet baseline. This is the pinned count of
# un-allowlisted fail-open swallows across the whole workspace (the
# `--all` scan). The `--ratchet` CI gate fails when the live count
# drifts from this number in either direction. Lowering it locks in a
# fix; RAISING it (to admit new swallows) still passes the script and is
# caught only by review of this file's diff. Regenerate after a fix with:
#   python3 scripts/check-fail-open.py --update-baseline
34
